==English==
{{wikipedia|cleric}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|LL.|clēricus|notext=1}}, from {{der|en|grc|κληρικός}}, from {{m|grc|κλῆρος||a casting lots, drawing lots}}, (Europe; many officers at Athens obtained their offices by lot, as opposed to election [''Liddell and Scott'']), from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*kald-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*klād-||timber, log}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*kola-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*klā-||to beat, hew, break, destroy, kill}}. {{doublet|clerk|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/klɛɹɪk/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɛɹɪk|lang=en}}

